1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,676
In Hosahalli, the old
school leaks every monsoon.

2
00:00:03,976 --> 00:00:06,993
And now a crack runs right
over a classroom door.

3
00:00:07,343 --> 00:00:08,243
Mrs.

4
00:00:07,857 --> 00:00:10,938
Lakshmi, the headmistress,
asks one question.

5
00:00:10,938 --> 00:00:12,751
Will my children be safe?

6
00:00:13,401 --> 00:00:15,712
So the town will build a new school.

7
00:00:15,712 --> 00:00:18,095
Two storeys, for six hundred children.

8
00:00:18,445 --> 00:00:21,244
Ananya, twenty four, is the site engineer.

9
00:00:21,244 --> 00:00:23,139
It is her first big project.

10
00:00:23,489 --> 00:00:25,215
Raghu is the head mason.

11
00:00:25,215 --> 00:00:27,937
Farhan, the surveyor, draws every plan.

12
00:00:27,937 --> 00:00:30,354
Professor Deshpande checks the design.

13
00:00:31,004 --> 00:00:32,833
So what is civil engineering?

14
00:00:33,133 --> 00:00:39,338
In 1828, the Institution of Civil
Engineers got its Royal Charter.

15
00:00:39,688 --> 00:00:41,801
It used Thomas Tredgold's words.

16
00:00:41,801 --> 00:00:46,319
The art of directing the great sources
of power in Nature, for the use

17
00:00:46,319 --> 00:00:47,970
and convenience of man.

18
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:51,530
Nature gives us gravity,
rain, rivers and rock.

19
00:00:51,880 --> 00:00:56,106
In simple words, civil engineers
plan, build and care for the things we

20
00:00:56,106 --> 00:00:57,006
all share.

21
00:00:57,559 --> 00:01:01,093
Let's watch the new school take
shape, one branch at a time.

22
00:01:01,443 --> 00:01:02,700
First, surveying.

23
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:06,176
Farhan measures the plot and
marks the levels with pegs.

24
00:01:06,526 --> 00:01:08,569
Next, geotechnical engineering.

25
00:01:08,569 --> 00:01:12,918
A borehole shows the soil layers,
so the footing is sized to suit.

26
00:01:13,268 --> 00:01:15,041
Then structural engineering.

27
00:01:15,041 --> 00:01:19,322
Columns, beams and slabs carry the
load safely down to the footing.

28
00:01:19,672 --> 00:01:24,128
Water and environmental engineering
add a tank, clean water pipes, and

29
00:01:24,128 --> 00:01:26,048
drains to carry waste away.

30
00:01:26,398 --> 00:01:30,768
Transportation engineering plans the
road outside, with a safe bay for

31
00:01:30,768 --> 00:01:31,965
the school bus.

32
00:01:32,315 --> 00:01:35,527
And construction management
turns it all into a schedule.

33
00:01:35,527 --> 00:01:37,706
Who works when, and in what order.

34
00:01:38,356 --> 00:01:40,640
Every building starts as a problem.

35
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:43,727
Civil engineers turn it
into a plan that stands.

36
00:01:44,427 --> 00:01:47,483
So civil engineering
has seven main branches.

37
00:01:47,833 --> 00:01:48,733
Structural.

38
00:01:48,718 --> 00:01:50,457
Frames that carry loads.

39
00:01:50,757 --> 00:01:51,849
Geotechnical.

40
00:01:51,849 --> 00:01:53,840
The soil and rock below.

41
00:01:54,140 --> 00:01:55,287
Transportation.

42
00:01:55,287 --> 00:01:57,494
Roads, railways and airports.

43
00:01:57,794 --> 00:01:59,121
Water resources.

44
00:01:59,121 --> 00:02:01,150
Rivers, dams and canals.

45
00:02:01,450 --> 00:02:02,529
Environmental.

46
00:02:02,529 --> 00:02:04,826
Clean water, sewage and waste.

47
00:02:05,126 --> 00:02:07,481
Surveying, also called geomatics.

48
00:02:07,481 --> 00:02:08,932
Measuring the land.

49
00:02:09,232 --> 00:02:10,936
And construction management.

50
00:02:10,936 --> 00:02:12,555
Time, money and people.

51
00:02:12,905 --> 00:02:16,273
Every real project needs
all seven, working together.

52
00:02:16,923 --> 00:02:18,912
Where do these branches work today?

53
00:02:19,262 --> 00:02:20,162
Structural.

54
00:02:20,103 --> 00:02:22,499
Professor Deshpande checks every beam.

55
00:02:22,499 --> 00:02:25,970
In a city, engineers design
the frame of a hospital.

56
00:02:26,320 --> 00:02:27,323
Geotechnical.

57
00:02:27,323 --> 00:02:29,632
Ananya orders a soil test first.

58
00:02:29,632 --> 00:02:33,926
On a metro line, engineers test
the ground before they tunnel.

59
00:02:34,276 --> 00:02:35,176
Water.

60
00:02:34,883 --> 00:02:37,587
Farhan plans drains for the monsoon rain.

61
00:02:37,587 --> 00:02:41,227
A city water board pipes
clean water to lakhs of homes.

62
00:02:41,577 --> 00:02:42,663
Transportation.

63
00:02:42,663 --> 00:02:45,461
The bus bay keeps children off the road.

64
00:02:45,461 --> 00:02:49,295
A highway project plans lanes,
curves and safe junctions.

65
00:02:49,945 --> 00:02:52,503
But is civil engineering always good?

66
00:02:52,503 --> 00:02:53,616
Mostly, yes.

67
00:02:53,966 --> 00:02:55,079
The good side.

68
00:02:55,079 --> 00:02:58,714
Safe homes, clean water, and
roads that connect towns.

69
00:02:59,064 --> 00:03:00,166
The hard side.

70
00:03:00,166 --> 00:03:04,275
Projects cost a lot, often run
late, and failures hurt people.

71
00:03:04,625 --> 00:03:07,116
Raghu wants to start digging tomorrow.

72
00:03:07,116 --> 00:03:09,866
Ananya says, survey and soil test first.

73
00:03:10,216 --> 00:03:11,950
Professor Deshpande agrees.

74
00:03:11,950 --> 00:03:14,570
A few days of tests can save a school.

75
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:19,745
India celebrates Engineers' Day on the
fifteenth of September, the birthday

76
00:03:19,745 --> 00:03:20,687
of Sir M.

77
00:03:20,687 --> 00:03:21,714
Visvesvaraya.

78
00:03:22,064 --> 00:03:22,989
The lesson?

79
00:03:22,989 --> 00:03:24,789
Check first, then build.

80
00:03:24,789 --> 00:03:26,589
Safety comes before speed.

81
00:03:27,239 --> 00:03:28,139
Quick check.

82
00:03:28,084 --> 00:03:31,134
Which branch checks if the
soil can carry the school?

83
00:03:33,034 --> 00:03:34,044
Geotechnical!

84
00:03:34,044 --> 00:03:37,453
It studies the soil and
rock under every footing.

85
00:03:38,053 --> 00:03:39,066
So, remember.

86
00:03:39,366 --> 00:03:43,563
Civil engineering plans, builds and
cares for the things we all share.

87
00:03:43,913 --> 00:03:48,332
It has seven main branches, from
structures and soil to water, roads and

88
00:03:48,332 --> 00:03:49,232
management.

89
00:03:49,502 --> 00:03:51,767
And every branch puts safety first.

90
00:03:51,767 --> 00:03:53,139
Check, then build.

91
00:03:53,739 --> 00:03:58,383
Next time, we'll look at the parts of a
building, substructure and superstructure.
